{#
    Ballot Terms - the overlay that asks how a vote should run

    Opens over the host form and closes again; the fields inside are part of the host form, so the
    answers travel with it on submit. That is why this modal carries no <form> of its own and,
    unlike admin/event/_venue_modal.html.twig, needs no endpoint of its own.

    Two ways to open it, and the parameters say which. Pass triggerId and value and a select opens
    it when it takes that value; pass neither and any element carrying
    data-ballot-terms-open="{id}" opens it on click, with confirm submitting the host form.

    Render it INSIDE the host form. A modal is a div, so nesting is valid; only the venue modal has
    to sit after form_end(), because it wraps a form.

    Used in:    templates/admin/event/edit.html.twig, new.html.twig, review/proposals.html.twig
    Parameters:
        - id        (string, required) - DOM id, and the value of data-ballot-terms-open on a button
        - terms     (FormView, required) - a BallotTermsType view
        - triggerId (string, optional) - id of the select whose value opens this
        - value     (string, optional) - the select value that opens it
        - title     (string, required) - modal heading, translated
        - notice    (string, optional) - an info line above the fields, translated
    Depends on: assets/js/ballot-terms.js
#}
<div class="modal"
     id="{{ id }}"
     data-ballot-terms
     data-trigger="{{ triggerId|default('') }}"
     data-value="{{ value|default('') }}">
    <div class="modal-background" data-ballot-terms-close></div>
    <div class="modal-card">
        <header class="modal-card-head">
            <p class="modal-card-title">{{ title }}</p>
            <button class="delete" aria-label="{{ 'ballot_terms.aria_close'|trans }}" type="button" data-ballot-terms-close></button>
        </header>
        <section class="modal-card-body">

            {% if notice is defined and notice is not empty %}
                <div class="notification is-info is-light">{{ notice }}</div>
            {% endif %}

            {{ form_widget(terms) }}

        </section>
        <footer class="modal-card-foot">
            <button class="button is-primary" type="button" data-ballot-terms-confirm>
                {{ 'ballot_terms.button_apply'|trans }}
            </button>
            <button class="button ml-3" type="button" data-ballot-terms-cancel>
                {{ 'global.button_cancel'|trans }}
            </button>
        </footer>
    </div>
</div>
